#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0467 expect=violation domain=SUPPLB
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when --STDTC is present in a Findings general observation class dataset, where its use is not recommended.
#note "EC-36 SUPP pin: on a SUPP/SQ dataset the -- replacement is the EMPTY string (Python wildcard_replacement), so --STDTC resolves to the bare STDTC. The STDTC column below is deliberately contrived — no shipped rule pairs -- with a genuine SUPP column (QNAM/QVAL/IDVAR/...), so this is the only way to pin the empty-prefix semantics against a real rule. Before EC-36 the engine looked for SUPPLBSTDTC and never fired."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset SUPPLB label="Supplemental Qualifiers for LB"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QVAL type=Char label="Data Value"
col STDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time (contrived — see note)"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | LBSEQ | 1 | LBREASND | Not done | 2014-01-03
---
